#!/bin/sh
# Stand-in for the codex CLI in live tests. herdr identifies it by argv0 and
# the terminal title: a braille spinner means working, any other title means
# idle. It echoes each input line. It does not model codex's UI or prompts.
printf '\033]0;codex\007'
printf '› '
while IFS= read -r line; do
  printf '\033]0;⠋ codex\007'
  sleep 0.5
  printf '• echo: %s\n› ' "$line"
  printf '\033]0;codex\007'
done
